course: dictionary
lesson: 10190
title: The word timer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A timer is a device that measures how much time passes. Most timers ring or beep when the set time is over, like a kitchen timer. Read the words around the word to find its meaning: «A boy in Vancouver playing a game puts a timer on, and when it rings he looks out of the window.» The timer rings, so it must be something that tells you when time is up.
explain: A timer can mean more than one thing. Sometimes it is a clock that goes off, and sometimes it is a part of a machine that switches it on or off at a set time. Ask yourself what fits: in «Lily sets her own timer, so the stop is calm», Lily is choosing a time for her gaming to end.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Countdown timers on offers are there to rush you» still makes sense if you think of a countdown timer as a clock that shows time running out. Good readers test a meaning in the sentence before they trust it.
fact: A timer measures how much time passes.
fact: A timer often rings or beeps when the set time is over.
fact: A timer can also turn a machine on or off automatically at a set time.
fact: «An hourglass» is a timer you can watch: sand falls through a narrow neck.
fact: On a microwave or phone timer, «1:30» usually means one minute and thirty seconds, not one hour and thirty minutes.
exercise: «A boy in Vancouver puts a timer on, and when it rings he looks out of the window.» What does the timer do? | It opens the window | It tells the weather | It counts the trees | *It measures time and rings when the set time is over
exercise: On a microwave or phone timer, what does «1:30» usually mean? | Half past one | One hour and thirty minutes | *One minute and thirty seconds | One and a half hours
exercise: «An hourglass is a timer you can watch: sand falls through a narrow neck.» Find and copy the word for a timer you can watch with sand. | narrow | *hourglass | sand | neck
test: Lily's mum says «no whinging». Whinging is Australian for what? | Gaming | Sleeping | Singing loudly | *Moaning
test: «Countdown timers on offers are there to rush you, so you buy before you think.» What is the purpose of countdown timers on offers? | To keep you warm | To show the time of the sunrise | *To make you feel hurried so you buy quickly | To measure how far you have walked
exam: In a kitchen, «Set the timer for 20 minutes» means what? | A person who cooks the meal | A cooking pan that heats the food | A recipe book with 20 pages | *A device that measures time and rings when it is up
